In this example, the concurrent_seq sequence activates two sequences in parallel. It does not wait for
the sequences to complete. Instead, it immediately finishes after activating the sequences. Also, the a and b
sequences are started as root sequences.
class concurrent_seq extends uvm_sequence #(simple_item);
a_seq a;
b_seq b;
// Initialize the sequence variables with the factory.
`uvm_create(a)
`uvm_create(b)
// Start each subsequence as a new thread.
a.start(p_sequencer);
b.start(p_sequencer);
join
