Since the scoreboard provides an uvm_analysis_imp, the scoreboard must implement all interfaces
required by that export. This means you must define the implementation for the write virtual function. For
the ubus_example_scoreboard, write() has been defined as:
virtual function void write(ubus_transfer trans);
if (!disable_scoreboard)
memory_verify(trans);
endfunction : write
The write() implementation defines what happens when data is provided on this interface. In this case, if
disable_scoreboard is 0, the memory_verify() function is called with the transaction as the
argument.

Once the scoreboard is defined, the scoreboard can be added to the UBus demo testbench. First, declare the
ubus_example_scoreboard inside the ubus_example_tb class.
ubus_example_scoreboard scoreboard0;
