4. Conclusion

A virtual sequencer is little more than a component providing a locus and scope to configure virtual se-
quences and provide handles to the subsequencers that will be required by virtual sequences.

The code for a virtual sequencer is rather simple. The subsequencer handles declared in the virtual se-
quencer will be specified, via the configuration database, after all components are built (after the
build_phase()) and are typically set by the environment in the connect_phase().

