Example 8 ‐ eth_pkt.sv ‐ pseudo Ethernet packet code

Consider the Ethernet sequence code shown Example 9. This simple Ethernet sequence randomly gener-
ates 2-4 Ethernet packets. The virtual sequences in Example 4 and Example 5 send this randomly gener-
ated set of Ethernet packets to the eth_sqr handle declared in the vsequencer component.

class eth_seq1 extends uvm_sequence #(eth_pkt);
`uvm_object_utils(eth_seq1);

rand int cnt;
constraint c1 {cnt inside {[2:4]};}

function new(string name = "eth_seq1");

virtual task body();
eth_pkt eth_pkt1 = eth_pkt::type_id::create("eth_pkt1");
`uvm_info("ETHcnt", $sformatf("** Loop cnt=%0d **", cnt), UVM_MEDIUM)
repeat(cnt) begin
start_item(eth_pkt1);
if(!eth_pkt1.randomize()) `uvm_error("RAND", "FAILED")
finish_item(eth_pkt1);
end
